TYPES.md §3.7: a public alias's body, and each arm of a public type function, may not name a local type; E2111 at each type expression naming one.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

local enum K { num, text }

local record Stone {
  n: Int
}

/// An event.
record Ev {
  /// Its kind.
  k: KindOf
}

/// The kind.
type KindOf = K

/// Stones.
type Stones = [Stone]?

/// The payload.
type P(e: Ev) = match e.k {
  num => Stone
  text => String
}
-- findings.txt --
error[E2111]  a/a.canon:16:15
  KindOf is public but exposes the local type K: make K public or KindOf local

error[E2111]  a/a.canon:19:16
  Stones is public but exposes the local type Stone: make Stone public or Stones local

error[E2111]  a/a.canon:23:10
  P is public but exposes the local type Stone: make Stone public or P local

3 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
